    {
      "heading": "ZFF talk: \"Can genius be taught?\"",
      "text": "Life Science Zurich is organising talks around three documentaries at this year’s Zurich Film Festival (ZFF). In this series, ETH Professor Elsbeth Stern joins neuroscientist and chess player Monika Müller-Seps for the talk \"Can genius be taught?\" to explain what happens to the brain during the learning process and discuss new approaches to learning.\n\nFriday, 30 September 2016, 3 pm - 4 pm\n\nZFF Festival Centre at Zurich’s Sechseläutenplatz\n\nInformation and live streaming on eyeonscience.org (in German)"
    }
